# ${name}

An oak starter project. FastAPI app wiring `oak.session.openhands.attach()`
per-request.

```bash
uv sync
uv run uvicorn agent:app --reload
```

## Shape

- `oak.workspace.create("local", ...)` - sandbox provider (swap for `"e2b"` in prod)
- `InMemoryStateStore` - single-pod state (swap for `RedisStateStore` in prod)
- `oak.session.openhands.attach(...)` - high-level per-request flow
- No lease, no trace source: enable both in production via `oak.session.configure(...)`

## Ownership markers

Code is annotated with:
- `[USER]`      - your application code; you own it
- `[OAK]`       - oak primitives / lifecycle plumbing
- `[FRAMEWORK]` - upstream agent framework (e.g., OpenHands SDK)

## Extras

The starter requires `oak[openhands]`. Add as needed:

```bash
pip install 'oak[openhands,e2b,redis,staso]'
```
